<task id="012" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>ACS provisioning: per-customer resource + Event Grid system topic/subscriptions (ADR-027)</title>
    <phase>W1 — ACS Integration (server-side only)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>7</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>003</dependencies>
    <blocks>030</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, acs, provisioning</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Extends the ADR-027 provisioning orchestrator with a first-of-kind external Azure resource (ACS) + Event Grid system topic/subscriptions wiring, with data-residency implications (immutable ACS data location → per-boundary resource). Tag `bff-api`; provisioning/infra surface; blocks the inbound capture path (030); publish-size + CVE governance applies.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-18</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add **per-customer ACS resource + Event Grid provisioning** to the Spaarke provisioning orchestrator (ADR-027), so a new customer boundary gets its own ACS resource and the Event Grid system topic + subscriptions that feed the BFF inbound webhook. Responsibilities:

    • **Per-customer ACS resource** — because **ACS data location is immutable at create time** (design §8.7, D-01), residency is achieved by provisioning a **separate ACS resource per boundary**. Add this to the provisioning orchestrator (ADR-027) alongside the existing per-customer resource creation, with the data-location parameter chosen per boundary.
    • **Event Grid system topic + subscriptions** — create the ACS Event Grid **system topic** and subscribe the relevant chat events (`ChatMessageReceivedInThread`, `...Edited/Deleted`, `ParticipantAdded/RemovedToThread`) to the **BFF webhook** (task 030's ingress), with a **dead-letter Storage** destination configured from day one (design §8.3).
    • **Document data-residency** — record that data location is immutable → per-boundary resource is the residency mechanism, in the provisioning notes / ADR-046 context (task 007 owns the ADR body).

    This is provisioning/infra wiring, not runtime message handling. Do NOT build the webhook handler itself (task 030 — subscription-validation handshake + Service Bus job) or the normalizer/persist (task 031). This task stands up the resources + subscriptions that 030 consumes. Align with ADR-027's existing orchestrator so this is an *extension*, not a parallel provisioning path (§11).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF architect for the Communication + provisioning subsystems, specializing in ACS server integration and ADR-027 subscription isolation. Authority on the provisioning orchestrator and `Services/Communication/Acs/`. Fluent in ADR-027 (subscription isolation / per-customer resource provisioning), ADR-028 (central credential; no `new` credential), ADR-010 (DI via `CommunicationModule`), ADR-032 (Null-Object kill-switch), §10 BFF Hygiene, §11 Component Justification, and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The ADR-027 provisioning orchestrator provisions a **per-customer ACS resource** (data location per boundary) and the **Event Grid system topic + subscriptions** wiring ACS chat events to the BFF webhook (task 030) with a **dead-letter Storage** destination. Data-residency rationale (immutable location → per-boundary resource) is documented for ADR-046. Provisioning uses the injected central `TokenCredential`/canonical management interfaces (ADR-028); no credential is `new`'d. Extension of the existing orchestrator, not a parallel path (§11). Build clean; provisioning-shape tests pass; publish-size delta + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Messaging inbound capture (030/031) depends on ACS emitting Event Grid events to a BFF webhook. Those resources must be provisioned per customer boundary: ACS data location is **immutable at create time** (design §8.7, decision D-01), so data residency is achieved by a *separate ACS resource per boundary* — exactly the concern ADR-027 (subscription isolation / per-customer resource management) already governs. This task extends that orchestrator rather than forking a second provisioning mechanism.

      The Event Grid path is at-least-once, unordered, and may duplicate (design §8.3) — the *handler's* idempotency is task 031's problem; this task's job is only to create the **system topic**, the **subscriptions** (chat events → BFF webhook), and the **dead-letter Storage** destination so failures are captured from day one. ACS management SDK usage is thin; measure the publish-size delta anyway (NFR-01).

      **§11 Component Justification (concrete cost-of-doing-nothing):** without ACS + Event Grid provisioning there is **no inbound event source** — ACS has nowhere to deliver chat events, so task 030's webhook has nothing to validate/receive and inbound capture (031) never fires; and without a per-boundary resource, the immutable-data-location constraint makes residency unachievable. The failure mode is a named contract failure (FR-18 unmet; 030 blocked; D-01 residency broken), not "future flexibility." This is an **extension** of the ADR-027 orchestrator (question 2 of §11 answered "extend, not new") — a parallel provisioning path would fork isolation logic ADR-027 already owns.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/DemoProvisioningService.cs (provisioning orchestrator surface — the ADR-027 per-customer provisioning to extend)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs + Dtos/ProvisionProjectRequest.cs (provisioning entry-point shape to mirror/extend)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/DemoProvisioningOptions.cs (provisioning options — add ACS resource + Event Grid + dead-letter config here)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Acs/ (from tasks 010/011 — ACS endpoint/resource identity this provisioning targets)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs (register any provisioning helper, unconditional per ADR-032)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory.cs (central credential precedent — inject for management calls, do NOT `new`)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-18">Provisioning creates/wires a per-customer ACS resource + an Event Grid system topic/subscription to the BFF webhook + dead-letter Storage; document data-residency (immutable location → per-boundary resource).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-027">Extend the existing per-customer provisioning orchestrator; do NOT fork a second provisioning/isolation path. Per-customer ACS resource honors the subscription-isolation boundary.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design §8.7 / D-01">ACS data location is immutable at create time → residency = a separate ACS resource per boundary; choose the data-location parameter per boundary at create time.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design §8.3">Subscribe chat events (`ChatMessageReceivedInThread`, Edited/Deleted, ParticipantAdded/RemovedToThread) to the BFF webhook; configure a dead-letter Storage destination from day one.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-05">Use the injected central `TokenCredential`/canonical management interface (ADR-028); MUST NOT `new` a credential inline.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register any provisioning helper via `CommunicationModule` only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">Registration is unconditional (Null-Object if feature-gated).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT build the webhook handler (030 — subscription-validation handshake + Service Bus job) or the normalizer/persist (031). This task provisions the resources 030 consumes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§11">State the concrete FR-18 failure mode prevented (no inbound event source → 030 blocked; residency broken) and answer the extend-vs-new question (extend ADR-027 orchestrator) in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§10">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta (baseline ~45.30 MB post-R4); no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/design.md</file>
