      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-032-bff-nullobject-kill-switch.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Extend the provisioning orchestrator (ADR-027)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/DemoProvisioningService.cs">
        Add the ACS resource + Event Grid steps as an extension of the existing per-customer provisioning flow; keep the isolation boundary ADR-027 defines.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Provisioning options" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/DemoProvisioningOptions.cs">
        Add ACS resource, Event Grid topic/subscription, and dead-letter Storage settings here; drive the create from options, per boundary.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Central credential injection (ADR-028)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory.cs">
        Resolve the `TokenCredential` from DI for management-plane calls; never `new` a credential.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read design §8.3/§8.7 (Event Grid events + retention/residency) + spec FR-18/NFR-05, and `.claude/agent-memory/researcher/acs-chat-integration-2026-07-16.md` if present. Read ADR-027 to lock the extend-not-fork boundary.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `DemoProvisioningService.cs` + `ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs` + `DemoProvisioningOptions.cs` to identify the exact per-customer provisioning extension point. Confirm task 003's ACS spike output (resource shape, Event Grid round-trip) and the tasks 010/011 ACS endpoint the webhook will subscribe against.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the ACS management dependency (Event Grid / ACS management SDK as required) to `Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj` only if a management call is made in-process; if provisioning is script/Bicep-driven, extend that path instead and keep the BFF footprint minimal. Record which path was chosen and why.</step>
    <step order="4">Extend the provisioning orchestrator: add a **per-customer ACS resource** create step with the data-location parameter chosen per boundary (immutable-at-create — D-01). Add ACS resource + data-location settings to `DemoProvisioningOptions`.</step>
    <step order="5">Add the **Event Grid system topic** + **subscription** steps: subscribe the chat events (`ChatMessageReceivedInThread`, Edited/Deleted, ParticipantAdded/RemovedToThread) to the **BFF webhook** endpoint (task 030's ingress URL, from options), with a **dead-letter Storage** destination configured from day one.</step>
    <step order="6">Wire management-plane calls through the injected central `TokenCredential`/canonical interface (ADR-028, NFR-05 — no inline credential). Register any provisioning helper in `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010), unconditional (ADR-032).</step>
    <step order="7">Document the data-residency rationale (immutable data location → per-boundary ACS resource) in the provisioning notes and as ADR-046 input context (task 007 owns the ADR body; leave a pointer, do not edit `.claude/adr/` here — sub-agent write boundary, root §3).</step>
    <step order="8">Write tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` at the shape/config level: (a) provisioning options carry ACS resource + data-location + Event Grid subscription + dead-letter settings; (b) the orchestrator invokes the ACS + Event Grid steps as an extension of the existing per-customer flow (assert wiring, not a live Azure call); (c) management calls use the injected credential (no `new`). Do not attempt live resource creation in unit tests.</step>
    <step order="9">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Provision`; build clean, tests green.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/msg-012-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline (NFR-01). If provisioning is script/Bicep-driven the BFF delta is ≈0; if a management SDK was added, justify any ≥+5 MB.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (focus: extends ADR-027 orchestrator not forks it, per-boundary data location, dead-letter from day one, credential injected not `new`'d); `adr-check` against `spec.md` (ADR-027 isolation, ADR-028 credential, ADR-010/032, §11 extend-vs-new). Resolve Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path — shared `Services/Communication/` + provisioning; coordinate with email-r4 + notification-spine-r1).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (012 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (in-process management SDK vs script/Bicep provisioning, event subset subscribed, dead-letter destination, data-location strategy, publish-size delta).</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
