  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The ADR-027 provisioning orchestrator provisions a per-customer ACS resource with the data-location parameter chosen per boundary (immutable-at-create — D-01), as an extension of the existing flow (not a parallel path).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An Event Grid system topic + subscription is wired to subscribe chat events to the BFF webhook (task 030's ingress) with a dead-letter Storage destination configured from day one.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Provisioning options carry ACS resource, data-location, Event Grid subscription, and dead-letter settings; tests assert the wiring at config/shape level (no live Azure call in unit tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Management-plane calls use the injected central `TokenCredential`/canonical interface; no `new` credential appears inline (ADR-028 / NFR-05).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Data-residency rationale (immutable location → per-boundary resource) is documented as ADR-046 input; no `.claude/adr/` file is edited by this task (root §3 write boundary — task 007 owns the ADR body).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Any provisioning helper is registered via `CommunicationModule`, unconditional (ADR-010/032).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; tests green; publish-size delta reported vs ~45.30 MB (≈0 if script/Bicep-driven); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on 003 (ACS spike — proves the Event Grid round-trip + resource shape). Blocks 030 (the webhook ingress consumes the Event Grid subscription this task creates). Parallel with 010/011 within W1 (distinct surface — provisioning/infra vs identity/thread ops).

    Strict scope: provisioning/infra wiring only. This task does NOT implement the webhook subscription-validation handshake, the Service Bus job, the normalizer, or idempotent persist — those are 030/031. If a step seems to require handling an actual event payload, stop — that is 030.

    Sub-agent write boundary (root §3): do NOT write to `.claude/adr/`. The data-residency rationale is captured as *input* for ADR-046 (task 007, main-session). Leave a pointer in the provisioning notes / `current-task.md`.

    Prefer the smallest BFF footprint: if the existing provisioning path is script/Bicep-driven, extend that rather than pulling an in-process management SDK into the BFF (keeps publish-size delta ≈0). Record the chosen path and its size impact.
  </notes>

